$ Deep-water wind-wave growth with the multiple DIA (MDIA)
$
$ Identical to quad_dia2 apart from the quadruplet treatment, so the two decks
$ isolate SWSNL4 against the explicit SWSNL2 of the default. Added for path
$ coverage: before this deck the repository never selected QUADRUPLET 4, so the
$ bounds-checked CI build never reached SWSNL4 or the per-quadruplet coefficient
$ cache in SWPRE4W.
$
$ The two lambda/cnl4 pairs are chosen to exercise the multi-quadruplet loop,
$ not to reproduce a calibrated MDIA parameter set. Like quad_mdia this deck
$ does not reach the accuracy criterion; read it as path coverage, not as a
$ verified physics reference.
PROJECT 'QUADMDIA' '001'
SET CARTESIAN
MODE STATIONARY ONEDIMENSIONAL
COORDINATES CARTESIAN

CGRID REGULAR 0.0 0.0 0.0 100000.0 0.0 40 0 &
      CIRCLE 36 0.04 1.0 34
INPGRID BOTTOM REGULAR 0.0 0.0 0.0 1 0 100000.0 1.0
READINP BOTTOM 1.0 'bottom.bot' 1 0 FREE

WIND 15.0 0.0
BOUND SHAPESPEC JONSWAP 3.3 PEAK DSPR DEGREES
BOUNDSPEC SIDE WEST CONSTANT PAR 0.05 2.0 0.0 20.0

GEN3 WESTH
QUADRUPLET 4
MDIA LAMBDA 0.25 0.16 CNL4 2.0E7 1.0E7
OFF BREAKING

POINTS 'GAUGES' 0.0 0.0 25000.0 0.0 50000.0 0.0 &
         75000.0 0.0 100000.0 0.0
TABLE 'GAUGES' HEADER 'quad_mdia.tbl' XP DEPTH HSIGN TM01 RTP REDTRIAD REDQUAD
SPECOUT 'GAUGES' SPEC1D ABS 'quad_mdia.spc'
TEST 1 0 POINTS XY 50000.0 0.0 S1D 'quad_mdia_sources.spc'

COMPUTE
STOP
